    "original": "Lordo scored at 66:40, and Arciniega at 82:49 to tie the game at 2-2.",
    "rewrite": "Lordo scored at the 66th minute and 40 seconds, while Arciniega did so at the 82nd minute and 49 seconds, resulting in the game being tied at 2-2."
   }
  },
  "final_span": "Oklahoma Christian versus another team at 6 p.m. Monday at the Hegi Family Arena in Oklahoma City.\nEL PASO \u2014 Despite goals from Belinda Lordo and Lino Arciniega, Western Texas College lost to Lamar South Plains College 3-2 in Western Junior College Athletic Conference action.\nLordo scored at the 66th minute and 40 seconds, while Arciniega did so at the 82nd minute and 49 seconds, resulting in the game being tied at 2-2.\nAt 49:49, Bri Thomas scored to ensure the Cardinals led from then on, and the Wildcats added another goal in the 82nd minute, resulting in the Cardinals having 21 shots compared to just eight for the Matadors. The Matadors, starting the season 7-0, suffered their first loss (9-1).\nNo. 7 WEATHERFORD COLLEGE 58,\nUBS INDIAN B",
